    {
      "bbox": [
        243,
        1471,
        1480,
        1715
      ],
      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "(d) Taxicabs and for-hire vehicles licensed as such by the Taxi and Limousine Commission are directed to pick up passengers from more than one location if such passengers are travelling in the same general direction. Each such passenger, other than a passenger seven years of age or younger or an attendant accompanying a person with a disability, shall pay a fare equal to the difference between the fare applicable when the passenger is discharged and the fare applicable when the passenger enters the vehicle.",
      "logprob_stats": {
